# Personal customizations are exempt from stylua.
#
# Why: the files under lua/custom/ use deliberate column alignment in keymap tables
# (rhs and `desc` line up so the whole block is scannable). Stylua has no way to
# preserve that — it collapses every run of spaces to one — so running it there would
# trade real readability for formatter conformance.
#
# The upstream kickstart files (init.lua, lua/kickstart/**) stay under stylua's
# control, which is what the CI check exists to protect.
#
# To opt back in: delete this file and run `stylua .`
lua/custom/
